      "type": "h1",
      "text": "3. Cleft sentences"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        4.6,
        6.4,
        6.0
      ],
      "head": [
        "Structure",
        "Example",
        "English"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "ser + subject + quien",
          "Fue Juan quien lo hizo.",
          "It was Juan who did it."
        ],
        [
          "ser + place + donde",
          "Es en Madrid donde vivo.",
          "It is in Madrid that I live."
        ],
        [
          "ser + time + cuando",
          "Fue ayer cuando lo supe.",
          "It was yesterday that I found out."
        ],
        [
          "lo que + verb + es",
          "Lo que necesito es descanso.",
          "What I need is rest."
        ],
        [
          "lo que pasa es que",
          "Lo que pasa es que no tengo tiempo.",
          "The thing is that I have no time."
        ],
        [
          "por eso... es que",
          "Por eso es que no vino.",
          "That is why he did not come."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "4. Absolute constructions"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Participle + noun, with the participle agreeing in gender and number. They replace a subordinate clause (time, cause, condition) and give a written, compact style."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        5.2,
        6.2,
        5.6
      ],
      "head": [
        "Structure",
        "Example",
        "English"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "participle + noun",
          "Hechas las compras, volvimos a casa.",
          "Once the shopping was done, we went home."
        ],
        [
          "una vez + participle",
          "Una vez terminada la clase, salimos.",
          "Once class was over, we left."
        ],
        [
          "dicho esto",
          "Dicho esto, terminamos la reunión.",
          "That said, we ended the meeting."
        ],
        [
          "llegado el momento",
          "Llegado el momento, actuaremos.",
          "When the time comes, we will act."
        ],
        [
          "dadas las circunstancias",
          "Dadas las circunstancias, no podemos.",
          "Given the circumstances, we cannot."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "5. Exclamatives and ellipsis"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        5.0,
        6.0,
        6.0
      ],
      "head": [
        "Pattern",
        "Example",
        "English"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "qué + adjective",
          "¡Qué bonito es!",
          "How beautiful it is!"
        ],
        [
          "qué + noun + más/tan",
          "¡Qué día más largo!",
          "What a long day!"
        ],
        [
          "cuánto + verb",
          "¡Cuánto has crecido!",
          "How you have grown!"
        ],
        [
          "vaya + noun",
          "¡Vaya sorpresa!",
          "What a surprise!"
        ],
        [
          "ellipsis: shared verb",
          "Yo como carne y ella, pescado.",
          "I eat meat and she, fish."
        ],
        [
          "ellipsis: answer",
          "¿Café? Sí, con leche.",
          "Coffee? Yes, with milk."
        ]
      ]
    },
